## Statement

A fair coin is tossed $10$ times. What is the probability of getting exactly $5$ heads?

## Hint

The number of heads follows a binomial distribution $\mathcal{B}(10,\tfrac12)$.

## Solution

The number of heads $X$ follows $\mathcal{B}(10,\tfrac12)$, so
$$P(X=5)=\binom{10}5\left(\frac12\right)^{10}=\frac{252}{1024}=\frac{63}{256}\approx0.246.$$
